            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              which presents this inclusion in that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an object in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant object
                  precisely if it is fibrant as an object of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  and in addition its image in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(C) \simeq Ho(\mathcal{C})
                  is in the inclusion
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Ho
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi Ho
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(\mathcal{C}^0) \hookrightarrow Ho(\mathcal{C})
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
                  precisely if under
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(L) \colon Ho(C) \simeq Ho(\mathcal{C}) \to Ho(\mathcal{C}^0)
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, prop. A.3.7.8
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              Use that by the above discussion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^0
              is the full subcategory on
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
              for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
              of morphisms. By the discussion at
              %span.newWikiWord
                Bousfield localization of model categories
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} ?
              this presents precisely such localizations.
          %h2#ExtraConditions Extra conditions
          %p
            Extra conditions on a reflective sub-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-category of relevance are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#AccessibleReflectiveSubcategory"} Accessible reflective subcategories
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#ExactLocalizations"} Exact reflective subcategories
          %h3#AccessibleReflectiveSubcategory Accessible reflective subcategories
          %p
            The following proposition characterizes when a reflective subcategory of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} accessible (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is accessible
          #LocalizationAndAccessibility.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} accessible (∞,1)-category
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    C
            %p a reflective subcategory. Then the following conditions are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  is itself accessible;
              %li
                %p
                  The localization
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Loc
                        %mo :
                        %mi R
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi L
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Loc : R\circ L : C \to C
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} accessible (∞,1)-functor
              %li
                %p
                  There exists a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi S
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi L
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi equiv
                        %mo .
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0 \subset S := L^{-1}(equiv.)
                  such that every
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
                  is also
                  = succeed "-local." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, prop. 5.5.1.2 and prop. 5.5.4.2, part 3
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p This is work…
          %h3#ExactLocalizations Exact localizations
          %p
            Recall that the reflective subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow} C
            is
            %strong exact
            – or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            an
            %strong exact localization
            – if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
            in that it preserves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} limits
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong
                exact reflective sub-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                \-category
              is a reflective sub-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-category whose reflector is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} left exact (∞,1)-functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} (∞,1)-limits
          %p
            Recall also that by the above results, a reflective subcategory is characterized by the collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi equiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = L^{-1}(equiv) \subset Mor(C)
            of those morphisms, that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            sends to equivalences in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            The following propositions say how the property that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            preserves finite limits is characterized by pullback-stability properties of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (recognition of exact localization)
            %p
              A reflective sub-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow} C
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has all finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} limits
              is exact precisely if the collection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi equiv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S := L^{-1}(equiv) \subset Mor(C)
              of morphisms that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              sends to equivalences is stable under
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %p So if for every pullback diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ′
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X' &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f'}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    Y' &amp;\to&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              we have that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(f)
              is an equivalence then also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(f')
              is an equivalence.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 6.2.1.1
          .proof
            %h6#proof_9 Proof
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              preserves
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(f')
              is a pullback of the equivalence
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(f)
            %p
              So it remains to check that, conversely, stability of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              under pullback implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              preserves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              preserves the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              and all
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %p
              Since the terminal object is evidently
              = succeed "-local," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo *
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L * \simeq *
            %p
              Next we check that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              preserves
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ×
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(x \times y) \to L(x) \times L(y)
              induced from the units
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_x : x \to L x
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi y
                    %mo :
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_y : y \to L y
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ×
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi Id
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                            %mo ×
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    x &amp;\stackrel{i_x}{\to}&amp; L x
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    x \times y &amp;\stackrel{(i_x,Id)}{\to}&amp; L x \times y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    y &amp;\stackrel{Id}{\to}&amp; y
                    }
            %p
              one finds that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ×
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %mo ×
                    %mi L
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times y \to L x \times L y
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                            %mo ×
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                            %mo ×
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    L x &amp;\stackrel{Id}{\to}&amp; L x
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    L x \times y &amp;\to&amp; L x \times L y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    y &amp;\stackrel{i_y}{\to}&amp; L y
                    }
            %p
              one see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %mo ×
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %mo ×
                    %mi L
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L x \times y \to L x \times L y
              is a pullback of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_y
              and hence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                      %mo →
                      %mi L
                      %mi x
                      %mo ×
                      %mi L
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times y \to L x \times L y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is closed under composition. Applying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              hence yields an equivalence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi L
                      %mi x
                      %mo ×
                      %mi L
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(x \times y) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} L x \times L y
            %p
              We now apply the same kind of argument to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              respects more generally pullbacks.
            %p
              For that, first notice that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                    %mo ←
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \to y \leftarrow z
              a diagram in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L x \times_{L_y} L_z
              of the image exists in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi L
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(x \; \times_y z) \simeq L x \; \times_{L y} \times L z
              it is sufficient to show that the natural morphism,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mi L
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times_y z \to L x \times_{L y} L z
              induced from the morphism of diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    x &amp;\stackrel{i_x}{\to}&amp; L x
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    y &amp;\stackrel{i_y}{\to}&amp; L y
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    z &amp;\stackrel{i_z}{\to}&amp; L z
                    }
            %p
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with the adjunction unit morphism on the horizonatals, is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi y
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mi L
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mi L
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi y
                                  %mi g
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi y
                                  %mi g
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi L
                                  %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Id
                          %mtd
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    x &amp;\stackrel{Id}{\to}&amp; x &amp;\stackrel{i_x}{\to}&amp; L x
                    \&amp;\stackrel{Id}{\to}&amp;
                    L x
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_y f}} &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{L f}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{L f}
                    \\\
                    y &amp;\stackrel{i_y}{\to}&amp; L y &amp;\stackrel{Id}{\to}&amp; L y
                    \&amp;\stackrel{Id}{\to}&amp;
                    L y
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow_{\mathllap{g}} &amp;&amp; \uparrow_{\mathrlap{i_y g}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\uparrow_{\mathrlap{i_y g}} &amp;&amp; \uparrow_{\mathrlap{L g}}
                    \\\
                    z &amp;\stackrel{Id}{\to}&amp; z &amp;\stackrel{Id}{\to}&amp; z
                    \&amp;\stackrel{i_z}{\to}&amp;
                    L z
                    }
            %p this may be decomposed as a composite of three morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mi L
                    %mi z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \times_y z \to x \times_{L y} z
                    \\to L x \times_{L y} z \to
                    L x \times_{L y} L z
                    \\,.
            %p
              If we equivalently reformulate these
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi y
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ×
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi g
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi Id
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi L
                                %mi y
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ×
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi y
                                  %mi g
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi y
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi x
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi Id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi L
                                %mi y
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                            %mo ×
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi y
                                  %mi g
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi L
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi z
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi Id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi L
                                %mi y
                            %mi L
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi x
                            %mo ×
                            %mi L
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi L
                                  %mi g
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi L
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    x \times_y z
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    x \times z
                    \&amp;
                    \\stackrel{\overset{g p_2}{\to}}{\underset{f p_1 }{\to}}
                    \&amp;
                    y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{Id}} &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_y}}
                    \\\
                    x \times_{L y} z
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    x \times z
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\overset{i_y f}{\to}}{\underset{i_y g}{\to}}&amp;
                    L y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{(i_x, Id)}} &amp;&amp;  \downarrow^{Id}
                    \\\
                    L x \times_{L y}  z
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    L x \times z
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\overset{L f}{\to}}{\underset{i_y g}{\to}}&amp;
                    L y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{(Id, i_z)}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{Id}}
                    \\\
                    L x \times_{L y} L z
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    L x \times L z
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\overset{L f}{\to}}{\underset{L g}{\to}}&amp;
                    L y
                    }
            %p
              It is immediate to check that the two bottom left squares are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              squares. So the two left vertical morphisms are pullbacks of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Id
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Id, i_z)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i_x, Id)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mi L
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times_{L y} z \to L x \times_{L y} z \to L x \times_{L y} L z
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              So it remains to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times_y z \to x \times_{L y} z
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi y
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi L
                                %mi y
                            %mi z
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi L
                                %mi y
                            %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    x \times_y z &amp;\to&amp; y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    x \times_{L y} z &amp;\to&amp; \times_{L y} y
                    }
            %p
              of the diagonal
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mi y
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \to y \times_{L y} y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              over the corresponding pullback diagram are equivalently diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi z
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp;  q
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \swarrow &amp;\downarrow&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    x &amp;\to&amp; y &amp;\leftarrow&amp; z
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;\downarrow&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; L y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              So now we need to show that the diagonal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mi y
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \to y \times_{L y} y
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              To see this, notice that it has a left inverse
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mi y
                      %mi y
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \times_{L y} y \to y
              %em this
              is in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              satisfies 2-out-of-3. But this follows now from pullback stability of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \to L y
              along itself.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (accessibility of exact localizations)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimits"} universal colimits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              (this holds for example if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is an
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0 \subset Mor(C)
              be a small set of morphisms, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              the smallest strongly saturated class containing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_0
              and stable under pullbacks. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is strongly generated by a small set of morphisms.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, Prop. 6.2.1.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topoi"} (∞,1)-topoi
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HTT"} HTT Prop. 6.3.4.6
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#inclusion_of_the_terminal_object Inclusion of the terminal object
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object+in+a+quasi-category"} terminal object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h3#cocartesian_fiber_over_a_reflective_subcategory coCartesian fiber over a reflective subcategory
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : C_1 \to C_0
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+fibration"} coCartesian fibration
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0 \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\hookrightarrow} C_0
              a reflective
              = succeed "-subcategory" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %p
              The restriction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1 \hookrightarrow C_1
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              if everything is modeled by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↪
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    D_1 &amp; \stackrel{}{\hookrightarrow} &amp; C_1
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    D_0 &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; C_0
                    }
            %p
              is itself a reflective
              = succeed "-subcategory" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
          .proof
            %h6#proof_10 Proof
            %p
              By the above proposition on reflectors, it is sufficient to produce for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C_1
              there is a reflection morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : c \to d
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D_1
            %p
              Such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is obtained by choosing any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+morphism"} coCartesian lift
              of a reflector
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(f) : p(c) \to \bar d
            %p
              To see this, consider for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in D_1
              the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi C
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo ,
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Hom
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi C
                                      %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo ,
                                %mi e
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi C
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi C
                                  %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Hom
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi C
                                      %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi p
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ,
                                %mi p
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi e
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi C
                                  %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom_{C_1}(d,e)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{Hom_{C_1}(f,e)}{\to}&amp;
                    Hom_{C_1}(c,e)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    Hom_{C_0}(p(d), p(e))
                    \&amp;\stackrel{Hom_{C_0}(p(f) ,p(e))}{\to}&amp;
                    Hom_{C_0}(p(c), p(e))
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By assumption
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(f)
              is a reflector, hence the bottom morphism is an equivalence. By one of the characterizations of
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coCartesian+morphism"} coCartesian morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a coCartesian lift means that this diagram is a (homotopy) pullback diagram. This means that also the top horizontal morphism is an equivalence.
          %h3#locally_presentable_categories
            Locally presentable
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
